{"id":"MB-0732","method":"rawSql","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:363","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Raw-SQL abstraction and injection safety are different properties; current regex also flags fixed SQL literals and does not resolve the connection type.","predicate":"In every parsed PHP/PHTML file in the declared complete custom-code inventory, database calls must resolve to approved Magento adapters/repositories and parameter binding; unresolved dynamic receiver or query construction is UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete source inventory","PHP AST and resolved adapter types","approved abstraction/binding policy"],"safe":"Bound Magento adapter query passes the binding policy; fixed SQL has a separate abstraction verdict.","fail":"Direct mysqli/PDO call outside approved adapter policy; concatenated request value fails.","limitations":"Interprocedural dynamic SQL and plugins require analysis coverage; this new policy does not prove no SQL injection."},
{"id":"MB-0733","method":"phtmlEscapedOutput","file":"TemplateRequestSourceChecks.php:247","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Regex recognizes a subset of echoes and any escape-function name; HTML, attribute, URL and JS contexts require distinct handling.","predicate":"Every output expression in completely parsed custom PHTML templates must use the encoder approved for its syntactic HTML/attribute/URL context or resolve to an explicitly typed trusted rendered fragment; dynamic contexts are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete template inventory","PHP/HTML context parser","typed trusted-fragment policy"],"safe":"escapeHtml in HTML text and escapeHtmlAttr in quoted attribute pass their respective context checks.","fail":"Unescaped dynamic output and escapeHtml used in a JS string fail the context policy.","limitations":"No browser/runtime XSS guarantee; Knockout/JS-generated output is outside this new PHTML policy."},
{"id":"MB-0736","method":"jsContextEscaping","file":"TemplateRequestSourceChecks.php:332","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Inline JS output requires nested HTML/JS parsing; finding an encoder name is insufficient.","predicate":"All dynamic output in completely parsed inline-script and event-handler contexts must use the approved context-specific serializer/encoder combination; unresolved script templates are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete PHTML/HTML inventory","HTML and JS parser","installed serializer contract"],"safe":"Correct JSON data serialization for script context including HTML delimiters passes.","fail":"Raw request output inside a JS quoted literal fails; unrelated escapeJs call must not suppress it.","limitations":"External JS/DOM sinks remain outside this bounded policy; no general XSS assurance."},
{"id":"MB-0015","method":"csrfFormKey","file":"TemplateRequestSourceChecks.php:276","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"An input named form_key can be empty and current detector passes it; server acceptance is untested.","predicate":"For the explicit discovered state-changing browser route manifest, automated integration tests must reject missing/invalid token without mutation and accept a valid token only with the appropriate authenticated session; incomplete route enumeration is UNKNOWN.","inputs":["machine-readable state-changing route manifest","isolated test deployment","session/token fixtures","transaction rollback or disposable records"],"safe":"Valid session-bound token succeeds in sandbox; public safe GET is excluded by route metadata.","fail":"Missing/empty/foreign-session token performs the state change.","limitations":"Run mutation tests in isolated environment, not as a passive production probe; this is route-contract coverage rather than all possible CSRF."},
{"id":"MB-0016","method":"ssrfSafeguards","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:959","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Timeout/allowlist words near a sink do not establish URL canonicalization, DNS rebinding handling or redirect controls across arbitrary application flows.","predicate":"For every HTTP-client adapter in the complete declared manifest, isolated automated tests must prove its approved destination policy rejects loopback/private/link-local destinations, DNS-change and redirect escape cases before connection, and allows the approved control. Unlisted adapters or incomplete network fixtures are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["source inventory","HTTP client adapter manifests","controlled DNS and redirect test service in isolated network"],"safe":"Known-safe adapter rejects loopback/private/redirect targets and permits approved destinations in controlled tests.","fail":"Adapter reaches a controlled forbidden target or unused guard suppresses a dangerous source sink.","limitations":"No defensible positive conclusion for the original broad requirement; arbitrary dynamic/network flows are not enumerated."},
{"id":"MB-0734","method":"unserializeSafety","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:523","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Current allowed_classes=false bypass is not sufficient for untrusted data; PHP documentation explicitly warns against it.","predicate":"In completely parsed custom PHP files, no invocation may resolve to native unserialize, including namespace aliases/fully-qualified and statically resolvable indirect calls; unresolved callable targets are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete PHP inventory","AST callable resolver","ban-native-unserialize policy"],"safe":"JSON decoder use passes the explicit native-unserialize ban.","fail":"Native unserialize with allowed_classes=false, true or missing option fails the policy.","limitations":"This is a stricter API ban with a new criterion; it does not prove all serializers and object-hydration flows safe.","sources":["https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.unserialize.php"]},
{"id":"MB-0735","method":"commandExecutionSafety","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:718","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Fixture shows unrelated escapeshellarg causes PASS for unguarded shell_exec; guard presence is not dataflow.","predicate":"No parsed custom-code call may resolve to shell-enabled execution APIs or backticks; only approved process adapter calls with literal executable and array arguments are allowed, unresolved indirect targets are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete PHP inventory","AST callable/dataflow analysis","approved process adapter contract"],"safe":"Approved process adapter with fixed executable and separate argument vector passes.","fail":"shell_exec of request input fails even with unrelated escapeshellarg nearby.","limitations":"New explicit execution API policy, not proof every OS command is semantically harmless."},
{"id":"MB-0019","method":"dynamicExecutionSafety","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:578","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Detector suppresses some unresolved includes/callables and interprets assert without installed-version semantics; current absence result cannot establish broad no dynamic execution.","predicate":"Completely parsed custom PHP must contain no eval, executable-string assertion, create_function or dynamic include target outside a statically resolved approved set; unresolved constructs yield UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete PHP AST inventory","runtime PHP version","approved include manifest"],"safe":"Literal installed-file include and ordinary assertion of a boolean pass the version-aware policy.","fail":"eval, dynamic request-controlled include and executable-string assertion on affected runtime fail.","limitations":"New precisely enumerated construct policy; dynamic language/runtime loading beyond analyzed files remains uncovered."},
{"id":"MB-0020","method":"pathTraversalSafety","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:781","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Nearby basename/realpath/DirectoryList strings suppress reports without proving canonical containment or symlink-safe use.","predicate":"For each declared file adapter and operation, isolated automated tests must prove all defined traversal, encoding, sibling-prefix and symlink fixtures remain within the approved canonical root; supported safe paths must work and incomplete adapter/operation enumeration is UNKNOWN.","inputs":["source inventory","file adapter manifests","isolated symlink and encoding fixtures"],"safe":"Controlled adapter rejects encoded traversal, symlink escape and sibling-prefix tricks.","fail":"A controlled read/write escapes the approved root despite nearby unused normalization.","limitations":"General path safety depends on runtime filesystem, races, wrappers and interprocedural input flow."},
{"id":"MB-0021","method":"uploadSafety","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:871","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Generic MIME/extension/size/storage words near a save operation do not prove enforcement or non-executable delivery.","predicate":"Every upload endpoint in the complete declared manifest must satisfy its exact extension/MIME/size/authorization/generated-filename/storage-delivery contract under isolated automated fixtures; unsupported endpoint architecture or incomplete inventory is UNKNOWN.","inputs":["endpoint and allowed-content manifest","isolated upload storage","test users","harmless MIME/extension mismatch fixtures"],"safe":"Manifest endpoint rejects disallowed size/type, stores under generated name and denies execution in sandbox.","fail":"Harmless forbidden-extension or oversized fixture is accepted contrary to its endpoint contract.","limitations":"Business allowed types, image transformations, virus processing and CDN/runtime execution are broader than source inference."},
{"id":"MB-0023","method":"csprngSafety","file":"InputSafetySourceChecks.php:830","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Current weak-PRNG detection depends on token-like nearby names; security relevance cannot be inferred from names alone.","predicate":"The complete declared security-token generator manifest must resolve to approved CSPRNG APIs with configured minimum entropy and no fallback to weak generators; unresolved flow is UNKNOWN.","inputs":["machine-readable security-token generator manifest","PHP AST/dataflow","entropy policy"],"safe":"Declared reset-token generator uses random_bytes at approved entropy with hard error on failure.","fail":"Declared generator uses mt_rand or silently falls back after entropy-source failure.","limitations":"New manifest-bound generator contract; cannot discover every security-sensitive random use by variable name."},
{"id":"MB-0737","method":"sensitiveLogging","file":"DataProtectionSourceChecks.php:930","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Source snippets neither enumerate downstream handlers nor prove every sensitive value is redacted.","predicate":"For the declared application logging pipeline and sensitive-field schema, synthetic canary values must be removed or irreversibly masked before every configured sink receives each defined event fixture.","inputs":["logging pipeline/handler manifest","sensitive-field schema","isolated sink captures","synthetic canaries only"],"safe":"All configured handlers receive redacted fixtures including nested fields and exceptions.","fail":"Any sink receives raw canary token/password from a defined event fixture.","limitations":"New schema/event-bound contract; unknown sensitive fields and historical logs remain outside tested coverage."},
{"id":"MB-0743","method":"sensitiveLogging","file":"DataProtectionSourceChecks.php:930","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"It reuses MB-0737 detector but PII classification is different; matching a customer/email word does not prove disclosure.","predicate":"For declared PII fields and event fixtures, every configured application-log sink must receive values transformed according to the declared masking policy; unknown sinks are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["PII schema","log sink manifest","isolated synthetic PII fixtures"],"safe":"Synthetic customer/email/address fixture is masked to the defined policy in all captured sinks.","fail":"A defined event sends raw synthetic PII to any captured sink.","limitations":"New bounded PII policy; no claim that arbitrary logs contain no PII. Share collection with MB-0737 but keep distinct conclusions."},
{"id":"MB-0746","method":"thirdPartyLoggingSanitized","file":"DataProtectionSourceChecks.php:895","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Third-party API responses and nested SDK log processors can bypass superficial redact-string matches.","predicate":"Each declared third-party logging adapter must redact all schema-listed secret/PII canaries from request, response, exception and retry fixtures before the adapter emits to its configured sink.","inputs":["SDK/logger adapter manifest","sensitive data schema","mock remote services","captured isolated sinks"],"safe":"Nested request/response and exception canaries are masked before emission.","fail":"SDK debug/retry logger emits a raw canary despite an unused sanitizer method.","limitations":"New adapter-contract policy; newly introduced integrations need manifest updates."},
{"id":"MB-0025","method":"magentoApiCryptoSession","file":"DataProtectionSourceChecks.php:960","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Raw APIs can be legitimate; framework name presence does not prove cryptographic or session correctness.","predicate":"Completely parsed custom PHP must use only approved crypto/session service APIs; ban a versioned exact list of raw session and obsolete crypto primitives, resolve aliases and report unresolved dynamic calls UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete source inventory","installed PHP/Magento versions","approved service and forbidden API policy"],"safe":"Approved Magento encryption/session service usage passes the explicit API policy.","fail":"Direct session_start or prohibited raw cipher invocation fails independently of unrelated framework imports.","limitations":"New syntactic/API policy; approved services can still be misused semantically."},
{"id":"MB-0094","method":"customAuthorizationChecks","file":"AuthorizationSourceChecks.php:393","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Current checker searches sensitive words and accepts authorization-looking names anywhere in the file, not executed denial paths.","predicate":"Every route in the complete declared custom privileged-route manifest must reject guest and disallowed-role test requests with no protected action and accept the authorized-role control in isolated integration tests.","inputs":["complete custom privileged-route manifest","test role/user fixtures","isolated deployment","side-effect oracle"],"safe":"Role matrix allows only authorized role and confirms no unauthorized side effect.","fail":"Unused isAllowed method does not prevent disallowed role from invoking operation.","limitations":"New route/role contract; object ownership and unenumerated business authorization are separate."},
{"id":"MB-0095","method":"apiExposureMinimized","file":"AuthorizationSourceChecks.php:255","verdict":"NOT_AUTOMATABLE","effort":"M","rationale":"Minimized exposure is a business decision about which APIs the storefront/integrations require; neither anonymous GraphQL nor public REST is inherently wrong.","predicate":"No positive automated verdict for original criterion. A separately named approved-route/schema allowlist drift check is possible after a policy manifest exists.","inputs":["business-approved route/schema allowlist","effective runtime API inventory"],"safe":"Approved public storefront route is not treated as a vulnerability merely for being anonymous.","fail":"Separate drift check reports an unapproved newly exposed route.","limitations":"The separate allowlist checker can enforce a decision, but cannot decide necessity or certify the original minimization criterion."},
{"id":"MB-0097","method":"hardcodedSecrets","file":"DataProtectionSourceChecks.php:523","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Secret pattern absence cannot establish that no hardcoded secrets exist; an active scoped pattern predicate already overlaps this topic.","predicate":"In the completely collected declared deployment source inventory, no literal matches the versioned supported credential signatures outside explicit secret-store exclusions; all unreadable/oversized eligible inputs make the result UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete source inventory","versioned supported credential signatures","explicit exclusions and redaction policy"],"safe":"Secret references and test placeholders pass only the documented signature policy.","fail":"Known realistic credential signature fails with redacted file/line evidence.","limitations":"A narrower new ID or existing MB-0730 revision/coverage expansion is appropriate; no claim that arbitrary unknown secrets are absent.","covered":["MB-0730"]},
{"id":"MB-0098","method":"unsafeXmlParsing","file":"DataProtectionSourceChecks.php:448","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Flags can be composed or supplied dynamically; current raw pattern detection does not resolve parser behavior/version.","predicate":"All completely parsed custom XML-parser call sites must resolve to a versioned approved parser configuration that disables external entity expansion, external DTD loading and XInclude; unknown flags/options are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["complete PHP inventory","AST constant/options evaluation","installed PHP/libxml versions","approved parser wrapper contract"],"safe":"Approved parser wrapper rejects external DTD/entity fixtures under actual installed runtime in isolated tests.","fail":"Effective NOENT/DTDLOAD/entity substitution or XInclude outside approved policy fails, even under aliases.","limitations":"New enumerated parser API/configuration policy, not universal assurance for third-party parsing outside collected scope."},
{"id":"MB-0099","method":"downloadExportAuthorization","file":"AuthorizationSourceChecks.php:519","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Route/file naming and login words cannot prove permission checks protect the exported data.","predicate":"Each download/export route in the complete manifest must reject guest, disallowed role and wrong-owner requests without releasing the protected test artifact, while authorized control obtains it.","inputs":["download/export route manifest","role/owner fixtures","isolated protected artifacts","response/content oracle"],"safe":"Authorized owner gets synthetic artifact; other identities receive no protected bytes.","fail":"Authenticated wrong-owner user receives another user's test export.","limitations":"New route/role/object contract; signed-link flows need explicit expiry/scope fixture semantics."},
{"id":"MB-0073","method":"httpsEndpoints","file":"DataProtectionSourceChecks.php:1","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"M","rationale":"Source HTTP literals are neither complete effective endpoint inventory nor proof of TLS enforcement; Basic already covers storefront HTTPS and mixed-content observations.","predicate":"For every effective endpoint in the declared Magento integration endpoint manifest, resolved production configuration must use HTTPS and the actual client configuration must enable peer/hostname verification; unsupported adapters are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["effective endpoint/adapter manifest","resolved production config","HTTP client TLS options","safe TLS test endpoints"],"safe":"HTTPS endpoint with verified peer/hostname passes; namespaces in XML are not endpoints.","fail":"Effective HTTP integration endpoint or verify=false client setting fails.","limitations":"New manifest-bound integration TLS policy; active storefront/mixed-content checks overlap but do not fully cover integration configuration.","covered":["MB-0026","MB-0029"]},
{"id":"MB-0075","method":"webhookSignatureValidation","file":"TemplateRequestSourceChecks.php:441","verdict":"SCOPED_AUTOMATION","effort":"L","rationale":"Finding hash_hmac/hash_equals/signature words does not establish correct payload canonicalization, secret binding, rejection or replay handling for arbitrary webhook providers.","predicate":"Every webhook adapter in the complete declared provider manifest must reject invalid/tampered/missing/stale signatures before side effects, accept the provider valid-event control, and satisfy its idempotency contract in isolated automated tests; unknown adapters are UNKNOWN.","inputs":["provider handler manifest","official provider contract/version","isolated valid/tampered/replayed event fixtures","side-effect oracle"],"safe":"Declared provider fixture accepts valid event and rejects invalid/replayed events before mutation.","fail":"Handler mutates state before verification or accepts tampered signed body.","limitations":"Provider-specific implementation is feasible per adapter but cannot certify the unrestricted original statement across unknown handlers."},
